<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Banat of Temeswar</h1><p class="st-meta">1718 CE – 1778 CE · capital Temeswar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Habsburg crown domain in the plain of the Banat, run directly from Vienna as a laboratory of colonisation and drainage after its conquest from the Ottomans.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-eugene-of-savoy">Prince Eugene of Savoy</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timisoara">Temeswar</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1716, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-passarowitz">Treaty of Passarowitz</a> in 1718 confirmed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a> possession of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mures-river">Mureș</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>. Rather than returning it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vi-holy-roman-emperor">Charles VI</a> kept it as a crown domain under military and court administration.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius-florimund-mercy">Claudius Florimund Mercy</a> rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timisoara">Temeswar</a> as a baroque fortress town, drained marshes, dug the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bega-canal">Bega canal</a> and promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> and mining. Tens of thousands of Catholic German settlers, later called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube-swabians">Danube Swabians</a>, were brought in alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanians">Romanians</a> and Italians, while Hungarian nobles were largely excluded. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a> was governed by a provincial administration answering to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1778 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> returned the civil <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> as the counties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temes-county">Temes</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torontal-county">Torontál</a> and Krassó, while its southern strip stayed in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/military-frontier">Military Frontier</a>. Its mixed population shaped the region until it was divided between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-romania">Romania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> and Hungary in 1920.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/banat-of-temeswar.jpg" alt="Banat of Temeswar" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: ThrashedParanoid and Peregrine981. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Habsburg_Monarchy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1718 CE – 1778 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Temeswar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles VI, Claudius Florimund Mercy, Maria Theresa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic and Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Romanian, Serbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Banat of Temeschwar, Temeswarer Banat</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1748&amp;focus=banat-of-temeswar" aria-label="Banat of Temeswar on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5183 565 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Banat of Temeswar lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5503 821L5381 747M5503 821L5398 749"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5381 747h0M5398 749h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5503 821h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5503 821h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1748&amp;focus=banat-of-temeswar">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
